Dear Zack,

I hope you are doing well.

I wanted to follow up on our recent discussions and share the attached
Scope of Services outlining the proposed relationship between you and
Renaissance Group. After considering the opportunities we discussed, I
believe there is a strong basis for establishing a relationship built
around shared business development, strategic opportunity identification,
relationship development, and mutual success.

The purpose of this engagement is not simply for Renaissance Group to make
occasional introductions or identify opportunities on your behalf. Our
objective is to establish a more active and collaborative
business-development relationship in which Renaissance Group can utilize
its professional relationships, broader network, market knowledge, outreach
capabilities, and strategic resources to identify opportunities that may be
valuable to you and then assist in developing those opportunities toward a
successful outcome.

Effective business development involves considerably more than identifying
a potential opportunity. An introduction by itself does not necessarily
create a business relationship. The opportunity has to be properly
positioned, the relevant parties need to be connected, relationships need
to be developed, and communication and coordination often need to continue
throughout the process. This is where we believe Renaissance Group can
provide meaningful value.

Through this relationship, RG would look for opportunities that align with
your capabilities, interests, objectives, and areas of operation. These
opportunities may include potential clients, contracts, projects, strategic
partnerships, investments, transactions, acquisitions, organizational
relationships, market-expansion opportunities, and other business
engagements. Where appropriate, Renaissance Group can assist with making
introductions, developing relationships, positioning opportunities,
coordinating discussions, supporting negotiations, and helping move an
opportunity from an initial connection toward a substantive business
engagement.

The 68 Smith Road opportunity is a good example of the type of relationship
and opportunity we have in mind. As that opportunity develops, Renaissance
Group may be able to assist with identifying and connecting with potential
buyers, facilitating relationships and communications, and helping support
the transaction as it progresses. It is simply one example of how our
involvement can extend beyond an initial introduction and into the broader
development and execution of an opportunity.

At the same time, we have intentionally kept the proposed Scope of Services
broad. The objective is not to build the relationship around one property
or one transaction, but to establish a framework that can accommodate a
range of opportunities as they arise. 68 Smith Road provides an immediate
opportunity to begin working together, while the broader relationship
allows us to pursue additional opportunities that may emerge through our
respective networks and activities.

An important part of the proposed structure is that Renaissance Group's
compensation is tied to successful outcomes. Where an opportunity is
generated, developed, or materially supported through Renaissance Group's
direct or indirect efforts and ultimately results in a contract, project,
transaction, investment, or other business engagement, the proposed
arrangement provides for a 3% success-based fee based on the gross value of
the resulting engagement.

We believe this creates a meaningful alignment of interests. Rather than
structuring the relationship around a traditional upfront consulting fee,
the model gives Renaissance Group an incentive to remain focused on
identifying worthwhile opportunities, developing relationships, supporting
the process, and helping move opportunities toward successful completion.
The more meaningful the opportunity we are able to help create together,
the greater the value for both sides.

The 3% structure also provides flexibility as the relationship develops. It
allows us to pursue opportunities of different sizes and types without
having to establish a separate consulting arrangement every time a new
opportunity arises. Whether the opportunity involves a property, contract,
strategic partnership, investment, or another business engagement, the same
underlying principle applies: Renaissance Group participates when its
efforts contribute to a successful result.

We also believe there is significant value in the broader network that
Renaissance Group can bring to the relationship. In many cases, the right
opportunity does not come through a traditional solicitation or publicly
available source. It can come from knowing the right organization, company,
decision-maker, investor, developer, partner, intermediary, or other
stakeholder and understanding where there may be a legitimate alignment of
interests.

As we become more familiar with your capabilities, priorities, preferred
markets, and areas of greatest opportunity, our efforts can become
increasingly targeted. The goal is to develop a consistent pipeline of
relationships and opportunities rather than simply pursuing isolated
transactions.

In addition to opportunity identification and introductions, Renaissance
Group can provide support with opportunity development, proposals and
presentations, strategic partnerships, market positioning, business
expansion, relationship management, transaction coordination, and other
activities appropriate to a particular opportunity. Where RG can add value
beyond the initial introduction, we can remain involved in helping organize
the relationships, communications, information, and materials necessary to
move the opportunity forward.

Ultimately, I believe the strength of this arrangement is in the potential
for our respective capabilities to complement one another. Your experience,
capabilities, relationships, and areas of operation can be combined with
Renaissance Group's network, strategic resources, and business-development
capabilities to create opportunities that may be more difficult for either
party to develop independently.

I have attached the Scope of Services for your review. The document
outlines the broader framework of the proposed relationship, including
opportunity identification, introductions, relationship development,
strategic partnerships, market development, business expansion, opportunity
tracking, transaction support, and the success-based structure of the
engagement.

Please take some time to review the document, and following your review, I
would like to schedule a meeting to discuss it in greater detail. We can
also use that conversation to discuss the 68 Smith Road opportunity, the
types of opportunities you would like Renaissance Group to pursue, and
where you believe our involvement could provide the greatest value.

More importantly, I would like the discussion to establish a clear
understanding of what we can build together beyond the immediate
opportunity in front of us. I believe there is an opportunity to develop a
relationship that is mutually beneficial, commercially focused, and capable
of generating meaningful value over the longer term.

I look forward to discussing the proposal with you and exploring how
Renaissance Group and your organization can work together to identify,
develop, and successfully execute meaningful opportunities.

Best regards,

Paris Swindle
Chairman
Renaissance Group
